<LegalLayout
  title="Workplace Policy — CG Design & Co."
  description="How we work at CG Design & Co.: remote work, flexible hours, pay, vaccines, equal opportunity and how to apply."
  pageTitle="Workplace Policy"
  lastUpdated="20 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    CG Design &amp; Co. is a small studio. Right now it's one designer, and
    as we grow, this is how we'll work with anyone who joins us, whether
    as an employee or a freelancer.
  </p>

  <h2 id="remote">Remote work</h2>
  <p>
    We're a remote studio. There's no office to come in to, and you can
    work from home or anywhere with a reliable internet connection. We
    talk over WhatsApp, email and video calls, and we meet clients online.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hours">Flexible hours</h2>
  <p>
    You choose when you work, as long as deadlines are met and clients
    get a reply within one business day. We agree a few hours a week when
    everyone is online together, set around your time zone.
  </p>

  <h2 id="pay">Pay and location</h2>
  <p>
    Where you live doesn't change what you're paid. Pay is set by the role
    and your experience, agreed in writing before you start. Employees in
    Australia are paid at least the minimums set by the Fair Work Act and
    any award that applies, including superannuation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="vaccine">Vaccine policy</h2>
  <p>
    We don't require any vaccinations to work with us. Because all of our
    work is remote, there's no shared workplace. You'll never be asked
    about your vaccination status, and it plays no part in hiring or pay.
  </p>
  <p>
    If a role ever involves meeting clients in person, we'll follow the
    public health rules that apply in that place at the time and tell you
    before you accept the work.
  </p>

  <h2 id="equal-opportunity">Equal opportunity</h2>
  <p>
    We hire on skill and attitude. We don't discriminate on the basis of
    age, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, religion,
    disability, pregnancy, family responsibilities or any other attribute
    protected by Australian anti-discrimination law. If you need an
    adjustment to apply or to do the work, just tell us.
  </p>

  <h2 id="equipment">Equipment and wellbeing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We provide the software licences you need for client work.</li>
    <li>You set up a safe, comfortable place to work. If something about your setup is causing you trouble, tell us and we'll help sort it.</li>
    <li>Time off is time off. We don't expect replies outside the hours you've agreed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="client-work">Client work and confidentiality</h2>
  <p>
    Client details, logins and files stay private and are only used for
    the job they were given for. Work made for a client belongs to that
    client, as set out in our
    <a href="/terms-and-conditions">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="applicants">Applying and your details</h2>
  <p>
    To ask about work with us, email
    <a href="mailto:info@cgdesignaus.com">info@cgdesignaus.com</a> with a
    few lines about you and a link to your work. We only use what you send
    to consider you for a role, and we handle it as described in our
    <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
